y do is so amazing they  helped us design these they got us  together with designers and we threw  ideas back and forth and we came up with  this  line and now we're happy to introduce it  and send it off into the world and a  hundred percent of the proceeds go to  variety boys and girls club so they go  that's so exciting i really couldn't  believe that when china like on said  that to us 100  100 of the proceeds go to building this  photography academy it was just a  no-brainer for us to sign on yeah i have  probably four of their tracksuits and  legitimately have worn them back-to-back  for three years their stuff quality is  incredible so cozy  they're so cozy they're so great so talk  about the design and and and really how  that came to be it's kind of a combo of  soup and pretty little liars talk about  that  yeah well i mean i the really exciting  thing about shine the light on was that  you know we have this incredible both of  us have these incredible fan bases um  from students and from pretty little  liars and we always are looking for ways  to engage our fans and to mobilize you  know them to do great things and also to  give back to them and say thank you for  being fans of ours so i think when they  came to us and said  what should be on the sweatshirts  it was you know we wanted to pay homage  to pretty little liars as you have on  yours and you know you can get a number  of different colors and different styles  um so we have the classic shush  and then um  suits we have i'm currently sporting  this one because i realized i really  wanted to start actually i was showing  off my suits fandom we have our  autographs on them which yeah which is  pretty fun  and then we did this one which is just a  camera that says the word variety in it  because we wanted to you know make sure  and remind people of what this was all  for and then that you know it started  with the main part is we came in and  said we wanted to do like a single line  drawing because we've been really we  have a friend who does them and she's  amazing at it so the last couple of  years we've just become obsessed with  like single line drawings so we threw  that at them and came up with these as  single line drawings and that was it  yeah  wow what impact did art have on your  lives growing i've got a little girl who  is just  lives eats breeds art it's just  something she was born it just seems  she's just hungry for it all the time  was that something for both of you was  that the way you were when you were  younger  yeah you know uh i was a pretty  uncomfortable anxious little kid and so  when i discovered the arts it was like  oh school doesn't have to be just the  stuff that kind of scares me which is  math and science which i was okay at but  it always felt very heady  um there was this other part of school  where suddenly i felt like i could be  myself like whatever was going on with  me was welcome and it was my job to like  figure that out and express it  and that was just like magical to me and  obviously we both you know  pursued careers in the arts um so we've  become  you know pretty taken with that  lifestyle but especially as a young kid  when you're in that zone of not really  sure what you're supposed to do or where  you fit or who you are in the world i  found that i like kind of became most  myself once i stepped into art rooms  whether it was visual art or  specifically obviously dramatic arts and  doing theater  i suddenly like became who i really  wanted to be and i think it has  something to do with like having the  freedom to express your situation your  feelings your thoughts whatever you're  going through  and specifically for me for photography  uh you know acting is a great art form i  love it but you really have to do it  with other people like it's not  something you can go home and do in your  basement or you know spend the weekend  just like acting by yourself like it's a  very community based thing which i love  but